  "paper_id": "ccs-2024-visionguard-secure-and-robust-visual-perception-of-auton-220b2cd7",
  "title": "VisionGuard: Secure and Robust Visual Perception of Autonomous Vehicles in Practice",
  "abstract": "Modern Autonomous Vehicles (AVs) implement the Visual Perception Module (VPM) to perceive their surroundings. This VPM adopts various Deep Neural Network (DNN) models to process the data collected from cameras and LiDAR. Prior studies have shown that these models are vulnerable to physical adversarial examples (PAEs), which pose a critical safety risk to the autonomous driving task. While a few defense methods have been proposed to safeguard AVs, most of them only target a limited set of attack types and specific scenarios, making them impractical for real-world protection.",
